  "issuedISO": "2026-10-28T09:01:00-10:00",
  "discussion": "A small northwest swell will continue a slow decline through Thursday then fade on Friday, but a small, short-period north-northwest swell will maintain small surf along northern shores during the next several days. A larger, long-period northwest swell will arrive late Saturday and may push surf above the high surf advisory threshold Sunday. The swell will shift more northerly and may briefly build further on Monday before dropping Tuesday. A series of overlapping south-southwest swells will continue through the weekend. The current swell is expected to produce surf above seasonal averages today, with an additional pulse late Thursday maintaining above average surf into Friday. Surf along south-facing shores will decline gradually this weekend into early next week. Surf along most east-facing shores will be dominated by wrapping north to north-northeast energy that could produce periods of moderate surf. Strong northeast winds and a large, rough north- northeast swell are possible Sunday night and Monday.",
